## 🔒 Privacy & Data Handling

### MCP Protocol Privacy Reality

**Key Finding:** MCP has **no built-in privacy controls**. Each server defines its own policy.

| Aspect | MCP Default | Our Approach |
|--------|-------------|--------------|
| Data exfiltration protection | ❌ None | ✅ Allowlist only |
| User consent | ❌ None | ✅ Explicit opt-in |
| Data encryption | ❌ None | ✅ TLS + at-rest |
| Audit logging | ❌ None | ✅ Full audit trail |
| GDPR compliance | ❌ None | ✅ We implement |

### Our Privacy Policy (Competitive Advantage)

**What we collect (opt-in only):**
| Data | Purpose | Anonymized? |
|------|---------|-------------|
| Pattern structures | Improve recommendations | ✅ Yes |
| Agent performance metrics | Benchmark comparisons | ✅ Yes |
| Trigger configurations | Discover optimal routing | ✅ Yes |
| Task content | **NEVER COLLECTED** | N/A |

**Privacy as a Feature:**
- "The only MCP server with GDPR-ready privacy by design"
- Clear opt-in UI before any sync
- One-click data deletion
- Published privacy audit

